1
00:00:00,639 --> 00:00:02,469
Hmm. It's kind of like
the Loch Ness monster.

2
00:00:02,641 --> 00:00:06,231
(Leonard:)Maybe there's something there,
maybe there isn't. We'll never know.

3
00:00:07,145 --> 00:00:11,065
(Leonard:)But sometimes it's fun to creep
yourseIf out thinking about it.

4
00:00:14,486 --> 00:00:16,656
(Mrs Cooper:)How are you doing
on the young Lady front?

5
00:00:16,821 --> 00:00:20,071
(Mrs Cooper:)I hear you're in some sort
of a long-distance situation?

6
00:00:20,242 --> 00:00:22,322
(Leonard:)Uh. Yeah, it's Raj's sister.

7
00:00:22,494 --> 00:00:24,284
It's kind of tough. She's in lndia.

8
00:00:24,454 --> 00:00:27,124
(Leonard:)Her parents aren't happy
she's dating someone white.

9
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:29,000
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, that's a funny turn, isn't it?

10
00:00:29,167 --> 00:00:33,297
Because you... You never think about it
going the other way.

11
00:00:36,174 --> 00:00:38,174
(Mrs Cooper:)Well, you can't force things.

12
00:00:38,343 --> 00:00:43,013
(Mrs Cooper:)Figure out if you're in a relationship or if
you're just calling it one. Like they say:

13
00:00:43,181 --> 00:00:46,851
"A cat can have kittens in the oven,
but that don't make them biscuits."

14
00:00:48,103 --> 00:00:49,773
That reminds me of another saying:

15
00:00:49,938 --> 00:00:54,358
"You can lead a chicken to Crisco,
but you can't make your mother fry it."

16
00:00:56,903 --> 00:00:59,033
(Mrs Cooper:)You pester me one more time
about chicken...

